ArchiveEntry "SMIB region of attraction H<4K (D,K>0)"

/*
 * Damped pendulum. The saddle is at delta=pi where H=2K(1-cos pi)=4K.
 * {H<4K} is positively invariant for D>0 -- the energy estimate of the
 * region of attraction (delta stays within (-pi,pi), no loss of synchronism).
 */
ProgramVariables Real delta; Real w; Real s; Real c; End.
Problem
  \forall D \forall K (
    D > 0 & K > 0 & s^2+c^2=1 & w^2+2*K*(1-c) < 4*K
    ->
    [{delta'=w, w'=-D*w-K*s, s'=c*w, c'=-s*w & s^2+c^2=1}]
    w^2+2*K*(1-c) < 4*K )
End.
Tactic "Proof" allR(1); allR(1); implyR(1); dI(1) End.
End.
